        "author": "Goharshahzad",
        "date": "2011-02-12",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0",
        "observed": "Inspected960×720 frontal courtyard picture:long red-sandstone prayer hall,three pale bulbous marble domes with taller central cap and finials,a raised central iwan/pointed recess,ten smaller pointed side bays,small open chhatri corner turrets and tall red octagonal minarets with projecting collars/pale open cupolas. Red paved open court and low perimeter arcades. Fine inlay/scallops,calligraphy,carving and current finish remain abstracted."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Badshahi_Mosque_courtyard_and_main_entrance.jpg",
        "author": "Taha 120",
        "date": "2014-09-20",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0",
        "observed": "Inspected960×720 closer prayer-hall/court picture:central deep pointed iwan framed by pale floral/geometric inlay and slender red pinnacles,flanking lower pointed arch bays and broad rectangular panel divisions;three bulbous marble domes with narrow lotus shoulders/finials,red crenellated parapet and open small cupola turrets. A low rectangular pale ablution enclosure sits before the hall. Model uses broad shared-material borders/closed recesses instead of copied art or an interior."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Main_Entrance_of_Badshahi_Mosque.jpg",
        "author": "Guilhem Vellut",
        "date": "2005-02-04",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-2.0",
        "observed": "Inspected960×720 east gateway view from Hazuri Bagh:raised red rectangular gatehouse with tall pointed timber entry,pale framed panels,inset side lights and upper open gallery. Four slender square corner towers carry wide-eaved open pavilions and pale caps;small ornamental finials/red crenellations,wide descending stair and adjacent low arcaded enclosure. Fine door art/inscriptions and exact stair/contact dimensions are estimates or excluded."
      }
    ]
